===Hosts and judges===
[[Tom Bergeron]] and [[Erin Andrews]] returned as hosts,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/Tom_Bergeron/status/633225253410447360|title=Twitter|last=Bergeron|first=Tom|date=August 17, 2015|access-date=August 18, 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160306015108/https://twitter.com/Tom_Bergeron/status/633225253410447360|archive-date=March 6, 2016|url-status=live}}</ref> while judges [[Carrie Ann Inaba]], [[Julianne Hough]], and [[Bruno Tonioli]] all returned this season.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.eonline.com/news/687433/dancing-with-the-stars-status-check-who-s-in-and-who-s-out-for-next-season|title=Dancing With the Stars Status Check: Who's In and Who's Out for Next Season?|last=Bricker|first=Tierney|work=E online|date=August 18, 2015|access-date=August 18, 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150819040700/http://www.eonline.com/news/687433/dancing-with-the-stars-status-check-who-s-in-and-who-s-out-for-next-season|archive-date=August 19, 2015|url-status=live}}</ref> After twenty seasons, [[Len Goodman]] did not return this season as a judge;<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.people.com/article/len-goodman-leaving-dancing-stars|title=Len Goodman Leaving Dancing with the Stars|work=People|date=August 19, 2015|access-date=August 19, 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150819220740/http://www.people.com/article/len-goodman-leaving-dancing-stars|archive-date=August 19, 2015|url-status=live}}</ref> in a video message during the finale, Goodman announced that he would return for [[Dancing with the Stars (American season 22)|season 22]].  [[Dancing with the Stars (American season 19)|Season 19]] champion [[Alfonso Ribeiro]] filled in for [[Tom Bergeron]] on October 5, 2015, while Bergeron attended to his ailing father.<ref name="Guest Host">{{cite web|url=http://www.people.com/article/tom-bergeron-alfonso-ribeiro-dwts-host|title=Alfonso Riberio Filling in for Tom Bergeron on DWTS|work=People|date=October 4, 2015|access-date=October 5, 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151006032051/http://www.people.com/article/tom-bergeron-alfonso-ribeiro-dwts-host|archive-date=October 6, 2015|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Leah Remini]] also filled in as co-host on October 19 and October 26 while Erin Andrews covered the [[2015 World Series]].<ref name=LeahRemini>{{cite web|url=http://www.eonline.com/news/707313/whoa-find-out-who-s-taking-over-for-erin-andrews-as-dancing-with-the-stars-co-host|title=Whoa, Find Out Who's Taking Over for Erin Andrews as Dancing With the Stars' Co-Host!|last=Bricker|first=Tierney|date=October 16, 2015|access-date=October 16, 2015|publisher=EOnline|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151017040324/http://www.eonline.com/news/707313/whoa-find-out-who-s-taking-over-for-erin-andrews-as-dancing-with-the-stars-co-host|archive-date=October 17, 2015|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Week7">{{cite web |date=October 22, 2015 |title=Scoop: DANCING WITH THE STARS on ABC&nbsp;— Monday, October 26, 2015 |url=http://www.broadwayworld.com/bwwtv/article/Scoop-DANCING-WITH-THE-STARS-on-ABC-Monday-October-26-2015-20151022 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151024222608/http://www.broadwayworld.com/bwwtv/article/Scoop-DANCING-WITH-THE-STARS-on-ABC-Monday-October-26-2015-20151022 |archive-date=October 24, 2015 |access-date=October 22, 2015 |work=BroadwayWorld.com}}</ref> There were three guest judges during the course of the season. [[Dancing with the Stars (American season 19)|Season 19]] champion [[Alfonso Ribeiro]] was a guest judge for week 3.<ref>{{cite web |last=Gomez |first=Patrick |date=September 22, 2015 |title=Alfonso Ribeiro Joins Dancing with the Stars as a Guest Judge |url=http://www.people.com/article/dancing-stars-alfonso-ribeiro-guest-judge-exclusive |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150923004537/http://www.people.com/article/dancing-stars-alfonso-ribeiro-guest-judge-exclusive |archive-date=September 23, 2015 |access-date=September 22, 2015 |work=People.com}}</ref> Former pro dancer and [[Dancing with the Stars (American season 18)|season 18]] champion [[Maksim Chmerkovskiy]] joined the judging panel for week 5.<ref>{{cite web |date=October 6, 2015 |title=DWTS 21 Wrap Up & Elimination&nbsp;— GMA |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pM02Ovv2O-A |access-date=October 6, 2015 |work=YouTube |publisher=Celebnews15 |archive-date=October 16, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231016214528/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pM02Ovv2O-A |url-status=live }}</ref> The following week, [[Olivia Newton-John]] appeared as a guest judge as well.<ref>{{cite web |date=October 12, 2015 |title=dancingabc Twitter |url=https://twitter.com/DancingABC/status/653734095000834048 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160309084307/https://twitter.com/DancingABC/status/653734095000834048 |archive-date=March 9, 2016 |access-date=October 12, 2015 |work=Twitter}}</ref>

=== Dance troupe ===
The dance troupe consisted of returning members [[Jenna Johnson (dancer)|Jenna Johnson]], Brittany Cherry, [[Sasha Farber]], and [[Alan Bersten]], and new troupe member [[Hayley Erbert]].

